            <div xml:id="d947">

                <pb facs="0990" n="870" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg870"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Bandit Activities, 1931/241:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-21T16:00:00-05:45">September 21, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:33 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>173. My 167, September 18, 3 p.m. The Acting Jefe Director of the Guardia has
                    informed me that no death sentences were applied in the case of the rioters at
                    Rama. I have discussed with him the Department’s attitude concerning the trial
                    of civilians and Guardia courts martial and he will take measures to see that
                    such trials are not held in the future.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
